const e='---\ntitle: EdgeLightBar – Menu Bar Companion for EdgeLight Overlay\ndate: 2025-12-14\ndescription: Lightweight macOS menu bar utility for quick control of EdgeLight display overlay – toggle, brightness, color temperature, and multi-monitor support.\nauthor: "cmalf"\nimage: /assets/img/Post/edgelightbar/edgelightbar.webp\n---\n\n![EdgeLightBar Preview](/assets/img/Post/edgelightbar/edgelightbar.webp)\n\n# EdgeLightBar – Quick Menu Bar Control for EdgeLight Overlay\n\nEdgeLightBar is a simple companion app that puts EdgeLight overlay controls right in your macOS menu bar.\n\nBuilt with Swift/SwiftUI, open-source under GNU GPL v3, no tracking or telemetry.\n\nRequires macOS Ventura (13) or later.\n\n### Key Features\n\n- Instant on/off toggle\n- Brightness and color temperature sliders\n- Multi-monitor support (all displays or individual selection)\n- “Exclude from Capture” mode (when supported)\n- Native macOS menu bar design\n\n### Download & Source\n\n- Latest release: [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/Cmalf-Labs/EdgeLightBar/releases)\n- Source code: [github.com/Cmalf-Labs/EdgeLightBar](https://github.com/Cmalf-Labs/EdgeLightBar)\n\nInstallation: Download the `.dmg` from releases, drag to Applications folder.\n\nContributions, bug reports, and suggestions are always appreciated.\n';export{e as default};
